DevOps Interview Command Series — Docker (Day 9) 🐳

Docker is the foundation of containerization.
From local development to CI/CD pipelines and Kubernetes — containers power modern DevOps.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Docker commands you must know:

docker --version
docker info

docker pull image
docker images
docker rmi image

docker run image
docker run -d -p 8080:80 image
docker run --name container image
docker ps
docker ps -a

docker exec -it container /bin/bash
docker logs container
docker inspect container

docker stop container
docker start container
docker restart container
docker rm container

docker build -t image:tag .
docker tag image:tag repo/image:tag
docker push repo/image:tag
docker login

docker volume ls
docker volume inspect volume
docker network ls

docker-compose up -d
docker-compose down
docker-compose logs

🎯 Interview Focus
• Image vs Container difference
• Dockerfile instructions (FROM, COPY, CMD, ENTRYPOINT)
• Exposing ports & networking
• Debugging container failures
• Image optimization & security best practices
• Docker vs VM comparison
